01:34:25.175 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
01:34:25.175   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
01:34:25.175   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
01:34:25.175   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
01:34:25.175   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
01:34:25.175   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
01:34:25.175   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
01:34:25.175   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
01:34:25.175   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
01:34:25.175   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
01:34:25.175   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
01:34:25.175   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
01:34:25.175   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
